\title{fmridataset: spatially typed, annotated fMRI datasets}
\description{
\code{fmridataset} keeps fMRI arrays aligned with what their rows and columns
mean. Its canonical container, \code{\link[=fmri_frame]{fmri_frame()}}, represents one observation
domain by one feature domain and carries stable IDs, annotations, entities,
relations, and explicit spatial identity through lazy views, feature maps,
binding, and storage round trips. \code{\link[=fmri_collection]{fmri_collection()}} groups equivalent
frames that cannot yet share a feature axis, and \code{\link[=fmri_study]{fmri_study()}} links
heterogeneous frames through shared entities and typed links.
}
\details{
Numerical values live behind serializable array sources
(\code{\link[=memory_source]{memory_source()}}, \code{\link[=nifti_array_source]{nifti_array_source()}}, \code{\link[=zarr_array_source]{zarr_array_source()}}, and the
sources provided by storage packages) and are read only on request, under a
realization budget. The logical frame contract is persisted through FDS
manifests (\code{\link[=fds_frame_manifest]{fds_frame_manifest()}}) and HDF5 via \code{\link[=write_frame]{write_frame()}}.

See \verb{inst/architecture/} for the decision records that define the data
model, the FDS schema, and the identity, temporal, and ID policies.
